From: Osborne Clarke <litigation@osborneclarke.example> (Solicitors for Mercon Steel Structures)
To: Ince & Co <litigation@incelaw.example> (Solicitors for Bluewater Energy Services)
Date: 2009-02-24
Subject: Bluewater / Mercon - SYMS Yuri Korchagin Field

We act for Mercon Steel Structures BV. Up until 18 December 2008 both parties had been working towards Milestone C6 on the basis that the SYMS would be completed subject to a punch list. Much of the work alleged in the Notice of Default was not work which Mercon had been properly instructed to carry out, and work could not properly be carried out in January 2009 because of the Christmas holiday, which lasted until 12 January 2009, and the winter conditions. Mercon's programme of 30 January 2009 was a satisfactory response to the Notice of Default, so Bluewater was not entitled to terminate on 3 February 2009.

Bluewater's purported termination is a repudiatory breach of the Contract. Mercon accepts that repudiation and the Contract is thereby terminated.

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: Bluewater v Mercon [2014] EWHC 2132 (TCC), paras 42-44, 129.
Only the fact of acceptance is recorded for this letter; reasons are Mercon's case as summarised at paras 42-44.
